--- 1. CLI Help ---
WX-1 standalone tools (experimental)

Usage:
  wx1 --help
  wx1 create-demo <file> <dataset-id>
  wx1 inspect <file>
  wx1 create-chunk-demo <file> <dataset-id>
  wx1 create-compressed-demo <file> <dataset-id>
  wx1 create-committed-demo <file> <dataset-id>
  wx1 create-generation-demo <file> <dataset-id>
  wx1 create-scientific-demo <file> <dataset-id>
  wx1 validate-scientific <file>
  wx1 read-array-slice <file> <variable-path> <start-csv> <count-csv> <output.raw>
  wx1 append-generation <file> <chunk-id> <payload-text>
  wx1 append-indexed-demo <file> <chunk-id> <payload-text> <variable-id> <time-index> <level-index> <spatial-tile>
  wx1 inspect-indexes <file>
  wx1 index-query <file> <kind> <64-hex-byte-key>
  wx1 inspect-chunks <file>
  wx1 repair <file>
  wx1 inspect-legacy-prefix <file>

create-generation-demo writes generation 1 with persistent chunk-ID, variable, time, vertical and spatial B+tree indexes. append-indexed-demo appends one chunk and explicit scientific ordinal mappings using copy-on-write B+tree updates. index-query performs an exact lookup with a 32-byte key encoded as 64 hexadecimal characters. inspect and inspect-chunks validate the complete generation and its indexes before printing. v0.3.8 (minor 4), v0.3.9 (minor 5) and v0.4.x (minor 6) generation files are supported. v0.4.x uses header minor 6 and metadata schema v2 for scientific arrays; inspect prints the scientific model summary. create-scientific-demo writes a synthetic 4x4 temperature dataset through the bounded reader-based codec pipeline. validate-scientific validates all scientific chunks; read-array-slice writes a bounded row-major raw payload without converting datatype or byte order. Scientific-model files are immutable at the metadata-manifest level and cannot be appended. repair explicitly truncates only bytes after the newest fully valid generation. Only one writer per file is supported; serialize append/repair externally.

